<title>GERMANY: Henkel Degussa stake sale yields DM520 mln.</title>
<headline>Henkel Degussa stake sale yields DM520 mln.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chief financial officer of German specialty chemical group Henkel KGaA, Ulrich Lehner, said on Tuesday that Henkel made net profit of 520 million marks from the sale of its stake in chemical group Degussa AG.</p>
<p>&quot;The net profit from the sale of our stake in Degussa AG, because we had to pay some taxes, was about 520 million marks,&quot; Lehner said in an interview with Reuters Financial Television.</p>
<p>The group said earlier that it had made gross proceeds of around 1.3 billion marks from the disposal of its 16.1 percent stake in Degussa to the German diversified utility Veba AG.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
